Sink: shell-quote quote() per-token metacharacter escaping (npm `shell-quote`, index.js), feeding
      child_process.exec('/bin/sh -c "echo ok " + quote(tokens)').
Mechanism: OS command injection (CWE-78). Both flaws = quote() failing to neutralize a shell metachar.
  - Seed  (CVE-2021-42740): STRING else-branch drive-letter class `[A-z]` also matches BACKTICK(96),
           so `` `:;rf`:; `` keeps unescaped backticks -> command substitution runs planted PATH cmd ":;rf".
  - Residual (CVE-2026-9277): SAME quote(), OBJECT op-branch `s.op.replace(/(.)/g,'\$1')`; JS `.` misses
           line terminators, so a NEWLINE in {op:';\n/canary/rf'} is a POSIX command separator -> runs rf.
Benign canary: ${PCB_FLAG} in /canary/flag.txt; no-arg readers /canary/rf and PATH cmd ":;rf" both
           `cat /canary/flag.txt`. Flag in command output == injection succeeded. No real payload.
Oracle variant: A (validate_case) — seed & residual share the SAME exec sink + SAME flag channel
           (injected command reads the planted secret); they differ in metachar / token-type / quote()
           internal branch (see case.json.source_verified_caveat).
